lines=['# Repaired-package red team — 2026-10-24','','**Verdict: hold publication. Five findings, six failing new warning controls, including two regressions introduced by the last repair.** Sealed target: `06e6a1384c94bd0c1298f0d50cfbe09ce3fc1bcf`. Review only: candidate, frozen questions, prior reports/evidence and sealed deliveries remain unchanged. This new review is outside the existing source ZIP.','','## Findings','','### F1 — High: reversed and implicit obligation wording loses warning scope','','`rebuild/tools/validate_packet.py:64–76,111,125–135`. `Attendance at these activities is a prerequisite for entry.` and `Only those who attend these events may take part.` are compulsory attendance conditions, but neither matches the obligation/dependency vocabulary. Neither has the punctuation/capitalization required by the fallback heading rule. The following personal-style official event date can be wrongly retained only in Section 12 without a missing-Section-6 warning. Original warns on both controls; preceding rebuild 3159bc2 and current rebuild suppress. Remaining regressions versus original, not introduced by the last repair. The actual A model replies correctly route the tested dates, so these witnesses establish a warning blind spot rather than an observed model omission in this pair.','','Acceptance: both wording directions retain operational-date hints across source records, with unrelated private and negated conditions still excluded. Do not treat a structurally valid all-12 card as semantically correct.','','### F2 — High: an unpunctuated conjunction hides a real deposit deadline','','`rebuild/tools/validate_packet.py:115–124,140`. `Our family reunion is August 2, 2027 at 7 PM and remit the official participation deposit by August 3, 2027 at 2 PM.` contains a genuine payment instruction beside a personal activity. The clause splitter handles semicolons/sentences and comma-plus-conjunction, but leaves this whole body as one clause. The personal cue then exempts the full statement; no remaining cue recognizes the imperative deposit instruction. Original warns; both preceding and current rebuild suppress. Remaining original-relative regression. Actual A model replies handled this whole statement correctly; the deliberately misrouted evaluator card exposes the missing safety hint.','','Acceptance: a personal conjunct cannot exempt an official deadline elsewhere in the same statement, regardless of comma presence. Retain wholly private combined-activity and contribution controls and every exact-copy check.','','### F3 — Medium: negated dependency creates spurious requirement scope','','`rebuild/tools/validate_packet.py:74–76,111,132`. Inside a private correspondence block, `Participation does not depend on attendance at our family reunion.` matches the new dependency cue despite its negation. This protects later private text and falsely warns on the birthday date. The correctly routed fresh rebuilt B reply reproduces it for S003. Original also warns; preceding rebuild suppresses. **New regression versus preceding rebuild, tied with original.**','','Acceptance: distinguish affirmative and negated dependency statements and prevent private nonrequirements from creating procurement scope. Positive dependency and genuine inherited mandatory-scope guards must still warn.','','### F4 — Medium: an explicitly excluded private subsection remains in official scope','','`rebuild/tools/validate_packet.py:79,128–136`. The source says `All companies must attend the following events; the subsection titled Private correspondence is unrelated and excluded from these activities.` The exact private heading appears in that sentence, so the lexical reference mechanism treats it as included and prevents its reset. A graduation date in the explicitly excluded private subsection gets a false Section-6 hint. Fresh rebuilt B reproduces this for S006. Original also warns; preceding rebuild correctly suppresses. **New regression versus preceding rebuild, tied with original.**','','Acceptance: a reference is not evidence of inclusion when its actual relation is exclusion. Preserve the positive nested-subsection guard and the genuine unrelated-private reset together. Do not simply remove inherited scope protection.','','### F5 — Medium: an annotated private heading still poisons warning context','','`rebuild/tools/validate_packet.py:87–89,126–132`. `Private calendar — unrelated personal correspondence:` clearly identifies unrelated private content, but fails the full-match private-heading pattern and enters the unknown-event-heading branch. The private christening date is then falsely protected. Fresh rebuilt B reproduces this for S008. Original, preceding rebuild and current rebuild all warn: an unresolved tie, not a newly introduced regression.','','Acceptance: body-supported private headings with explanatory annotations should not become requirement headings solely because they contain calendar/events vocabulary. Clinical or officially compulsory content must retain hints.','','## Frozen method','','The 17 controls, three fixtures, selected semantic expectations and source hashes were committed in `40dede9` before execution. Complete original model baseline committed in `ba50915` before rebuilt calls. Unchanged canonical tools/run_arm.py, gpt-6-astra medium, same A/B/C order, same six-file knowledge selection, fresh ephemeral sessions, no tools, retries, corrections or best-of selection. Expected answers were not supplied to models. Canonical prompts, command flags, metadata, tool-free events and exact raw-card equality are verified in model-audit.json and model-results.json. Host system messages are not held byte-identical.','','The middle comparator is the exact preserved 3159bc2 validator, used only for evaluator-card controls and same-card replay; there is no third model arm. Cases are targeted synthetic probes informed by the code and past findings, not independent real-world validation. Unknown source anchors are valid under the shipped source grammar. Candidate code and model knowledge were not changed.','','## New evaluator controls','','| Validator | Passed | Failed |','|---|---:|---:|']
