lines+=['','The six current failures are F1 two, and F2–F5 one each. Three unsafe-suppression controls regress relative to original. Two false-warning controls regress relative to the preceding rebuild. F5 fails all three versions. Aggregate counts are specific to this selected set and do not establish a population reliability estimate.','','The official all-12 cards intentionally omit operational dates; the personal all-12 cards are correct. These are evaluator-built controls, not model replies. Every warning control is structurally valid and exits 0, so exit status alone cannot grade relevance. Full per-case comparisons, commands, stdout, stderr and exit codes are preserved under controls/ and control-results.json.','','## Fresh model pair','','| Fixture | Original | Rebuild | Interpretation |','|---|---|---|---|','| A: reversed/implicit obligations and mixed conjunction | Targeted routing and fidelity PASS | Targeted routing and fidelity PASS | Tie; warning controls expose blind spots despite this pair’s correct routing |','| B: negated dependency and private headings | Personal S002 leaks to 4/6; S003/S006/S008 leak to 6 | All seven selected private records only in 12; false warning IDs S003/S006/S008 | Routing improves; warning accuracy still fails |','| C: six new opaque citation forms | Required 4/5 placement and exact copies PASS | Required 4/5 placement and exact copies PASS | Tie; no observed citation regression |','','All six replies pass the common strict fidelity/shape gate. Selected semantic checks pass original 2/3, rebuild 3/3; combined checks pass 2/3 in each arm because B fails for different reasons. This combined tie must not conceal the improved model routing or the rebuilt tool’s false warnings. Selected checks do not exhaustively grade every header or extra semantic placement.','','The exact same raw rebuilt B card was replayed under all three validators in same-card-warning-replay.json. Same source and card hashes, no output edits or model rerun: original hints S003/S006/S008; preceding hints only S008; current hints S003/S006/S008. That isolates the two newly introduced warning regressions from model variability.','','## Citation variants','','No new citation finding on these tests. Both model arms copy all six anchors exactly. All three validators accept the exact combined control and reject each of six mutations: variation-selector deletion, combining-grapheme-joiner deletion, narrow-NBSP replacement, quote-entity decoding, soft-hyphen deletion and fullwidth-Latin-letter normalization. The anchor with an embedded `[source: note]` fragment is preserved as a complete opaque anchor. These passes are ties, not improvements. They do not establish universal Unicode-copying reliability or erase older preserved citation failures.','','## Existing full RFP and competition specification','','Read-only replay of the latest scope-guard-repair full-RFP evidence preserves its result: rebuilt native validation passes, all selected required/forbidden routing checks pass, and S215–S221 remain only in Section 12. Original still leaks six personal records and misses S133 in 11, S066/S083 in 5 and S148 in 11. No new full-length model calls or replacement historical scores were made. See full-recheck.json. Frozen-question scores remain the prior five improvements/three ties; they were not freshly rerun in this review.','','The competition asks for visible closure of the actual feedback and honest reporting of ties/regressions. F3–F5 directly affect the personal-content/no-spurious-warning request. F1/F2 show that personal suppression can still hide real deadline hints. The sealed report already limits its claims to recorded controls and a finite heuristic: these new cases narrow confidence beyond that coverage rather than invalidating its earlier recorded passes. Reconcile the next submission report and package with these findings before publication.','','No new formal layout/sequence or submission-length defect is asserted. Original pin, feedback, pre-rebuild frozen questions, paired evidence and history are retained. Current draft is three sentences, within the supplied 2–3 sentence requirement. Premium/VIP eligibility and a valid public repository URL remain unverified. The supplied deadline is Wednesday October 28, 11:59 PM EST. No publication occurred.','','## What could still cost the win','','1. Warning polarity and scope remain brittle: merely mentioning a private heading can override an explicit exclusion, and a negated dependency can act like an obligation. Both are reproduced on one actual correct model card.','2. Personal support is checked per syntactically parsed chunk, so common unpunctuated mixed wording can still evade the intended conservative boundary.','3. The six model knowledge files are unchanged. Fresh-draw improvements do not demonstrate a new routing-prompt repair, and the automated OpenAI harness is not fresh Claude/judge acceptance.','4. Passing historical controls and one full RFP cannot establish unseen-case reliability. The 21,696-file sealed source also imposes review burden; keep the evidence map and current verdict clear.','5. Administrative submission conditions remain open. The current sealed ZIP does not include this new review; it should not be represented as incorporating these findings.','','## Evidence preservation and delivery','','preservation-verification.json confirms all 21,696 prior tracked files and 41 sealed files unchanged, frozen questions byte-identical to bfdd812, and the preceding validator snapshot exact. All fresh definitions, requests, raw events/cards, audits, control failures and comparisons are preserved in this new directory. Candidate, root reports and deliveries were not edited or replaced.','','delivery-summary.json records the new fresh-clone audit when complete; delivery-checks.json retains every command and any failure. Mechanical archive/history compliance is separate from the warning findings. No fixes or publication performed.','']
